    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"teams - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/teams.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [teams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: Workers and the tasks they can do, as a bipartite graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [teams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: Workers and the tasks they can do, as a bipartite graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [teams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Workers and the tasks they can do, as a bipartite graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nWorkers and the tasks they can do, as a bipartite graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L739-L824){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nteams(contractor=False)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nA made-up software team of 8 workers and the 8 tasks of a release, with an edge from each\nworker to every task they can do, weighted by the hours it would take them. Giving every\ntask its own worker is a matching problem, and doing it in the fewest total hours is the\nassignment problem. The team is one person short, so set `contractor=True` to hire Quinn,\na contractor who can take on security or DevOps.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 16 nodes (8 workers, then 8 tasks, labeled by name), or 17 with the contractor\n- 21 edges (who can do what), or 23 with the contractor\n- Undirected, bipartite, weighted by hours\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `side`: `\"worker\"` or `\"task\"`\n- `role`: the worker's job, `\"Engineer\"`, `\"Designer\"`, `\"Writer\"`, `\"Tester\"` or\n  `\"Contractor\"` (missing for tasks)\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `hours`: how long the worker would take on the task, the same as the edge weight\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **One task too many.** Only Omar and Kofi can do any of Database, DevOps and Security,\n  and two people can't take three tasks (Hall's condition fails), so at most 7 of the 8\n  tasks can be covered and `bipartite_minimum_weight_full_matching()` raises an error.\n- **The contractor fixes it.** With `contractor=True` every task can be covered, and the\n  cheapest assignment is unique: 37 hours, with Quinn on DevOps, Kofi on Security, Omar on\n  Database, and Luis, one of the two designers, left free. The next best takes 38.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[contractor]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to add the contractor Quinn, who can do the `\"Security\"` task in 4 hours or the\n    `\"DevOps\"` task in 5. Default is `False`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The bipartite graph of workers and tasks.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the workers and tasks, colored by side:\n\n::: {#8af07e88 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nteam = ec.teams()\n\nteam.plot(color_by=\"side\", label_by=\"label\", seed=4)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"13.2 -11.4 760.0 542.9\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, san